// Copy this file to Sentry.xcconfig and set your real DSN there.
//
// Sentry.xcconfig is gitignored. The DSN must NEVER be committed, and never go
// in a .xcscheme (it leaked that way once, #10). For App Store / Xcode Cloud
// builds, supply the DSN another way (an Xcode Cloud environment variable, or a
// ci_post_clone script that writes this file with the same escaping as below).
//
// IMPORTANT: an xcconfig treats "//" as the start of a comment, so a DSN written
// plainly as https://... is silently cut down to "https:". Escape the slashes as
// "/$()/" ($() expands to nothing at build time), for example:
//
//   SENTRY_DSN = https:/$()/examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
//
// An empty DSN keeps Sentry inactive (fine for CI and local Debug builds). A
// Release build whose DSN is empty or not a full https://...@... value fails on
// purpose (see the "Verify Sentry DSN for Release" build phase), so a shipped
// build cannot silently lose crash reports.
SENTRY_DSN =
